        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "The article argues that conventional technology metricsΓÇöspeed, cost reduction, and adoption ratesΓÇöare fundamentally mismatched for evaluating AI value because they were designed for fixed-capability software. Speed metrics miss organizational bottlenecks and discourage quality checking; cost reduction has a ceiling equal to current spend; adoption metrics reward shallow use over high-value judgment applications. The author proposes six alternative signals: declining review burden, shared corrections, new work capabilities, expanding delegation, falling cost-per-verified-outcome, and deepening usage patterns.",
