        "summary":  "Security firm Pillar Security discovered two critical vulnerabilities in Google\u0027s Agent Development Kit (ADK) for Python: a triage agent exploit allowing malicious pull requests to hijack CI/CD workflows with collaborator privileges, and an antigravity agent exploit enabling prompt injection through public issues to exfiltrate Google Cloud service account credentials. Security experts warn that in multi-agent systems, an agent\u0027s risk extends to every higher-privilege system its output can influenceΓÇönot just its assigned tools.",
